# ⭐ Quick Revision Table

| Problem   | Main Logic                   |
| --------- | ---------------------------- |
| Count     | `count++`                    |
| Sum       | `sum += value`               |
| Maximum   | `max = Math.max(max, value)` |
| Frequency | `frequency[value]++`         |
| Prime     | `n % i == 0`                 |
| GCD       | `a % b` repeatedly           |
| LCM       | `(a / gcd(a,b)) * b`         |

# 🧠 Remember These Patterns

```java
// COUNT
count++;

// SUM
sum += value;

// MAXIMUM
max = Math.max(max, value);

// FREQUENCY
frequency[value]++;

// PRIME
for (int i = 2; i * i <= n; i++) {
    if (n % i == 0) {
        prime = false;
        break;
    }
}

// GCD
while (b != 0) {
    int temp = a % b;
    a = b;
    b = temp;
}

// LCM
(long) a / gcd(a, b) * b;
```

These are **core DSA patterns**. Many beginner/intermediate problems are just combinations of these patterns.
